WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.710
Geometry is around us all the time!

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:12.950
It is so intricately involved in our day-to-
day life that we don’t even notice it.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.549
How, you may ask?

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:20.529
Imagine that we were walking in a straight
line for one kilometre.

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:24.410
After that,
we turn left and walk 1 kilometre in this

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.410
direction.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:31.550
Then again, we turn left and
walk 1 kilometre in this direction.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.270
Now for the last time we turn left and walk
1

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.270
kilometre.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.100
We would find that we are at the same place
we started from!

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.020
If we
trace our route, we would find that we walked

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.890
in a SQUARE shaped route!

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.900
This was only ONE example.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.630
Geometry is hidden in natural patterns too!

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:56.520
Have you noticed the seeds in a
sunflower?

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.470
If you look closely, they form a spiral shaped
design.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:04.360
Do you know
any other examples where you notice a spiral

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.100
pattern?

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.250
I know one…

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.780
spiral
galaxies!

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.990
These are types of galaxies that have a spiral
pattern, similar to our

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.859
sunflower seeds.

00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:19.520
So we see that geometry is involved in things
as small as

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.749
sunflower seeds to things as big as galaxies!

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:28.679
Don’t you think it would be fun to study
these Geometrical shapes?

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:32.840
We have a very long history with the knowledge
of geometry.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.560
From ancient
times, people were aware of geometry and used

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.229
it in their day-to-day life.

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:43.369
***
Let’s take an example of ancient Egypt.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:48.210
Long ago, the people of ancient Egypt faced
a problem every year.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.859
The
problem was that the Nile river used to flood

00:01:51.859 --> 00:01:53.709
each year.

00:01:53.709 --> 00:01:56.679
And whenever it
flooded, it used to destroy the boundaries

00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:59.780
of land near the banks of the river.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.810
This used to put the landowners in a problem!

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.920
After the flood, the boundaries
of lands would dissolve away.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.760
So nobody would know which part of land
belonged to whom, and this would result in

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.780
confusion!

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.360
As this was an annual problem, they came up
with a system of measuring land

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.180
and redistributing it to the respective owners
after the flood.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.560
This system of
measuring was one of the factors that gave

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:32.350
birth to the word GEOMETRY
which we study today.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:37.750
The Indus Valley civilization around the year
3000 BCE also made use of

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.760
geometry.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.460
Their cities were well planned, houses had
different types of rooms,

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.660
well planned roads and a good drainage system.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.160
This was not possible if they
did not know the use of geometry.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.761
Basically, geometry was being used in many
parts of the world throughout the

00:02:56.761 --> 00:02:59.210
period.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.010
The word GEOMETRY itself comes from the combination
of Greek words

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:08.630
“GEO” meaning LAND or EARTH, and “METREIN”
meaning MEASUREMENT.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.020
So
GEOMETRY means the measurement of earth.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:17.370
The geometry we study on paper today, was
actually conceived as a solution

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:21.320
for day-to-day problems in the ancient world.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.920
The ancient Egyptians also used
geometry in construction, designing granaries

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.510
and making the pyramids!

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:33.980
So, all the existing knowledge about geometry
was brought together in a form

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.680
of a book by Euclid.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.710
Euclid was a Greek mathematician who used
to teach

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:45.360
mathematics in the city of Alexandria, in
Egypt.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.510
He was the first person to
collect all the work done on geometry and

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.340
put it together in books
called ‘Elements’.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:04:00.090
His book contains definitions, axioms, postulates,
and proofs that we can use

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.490
to prove things further ahead in complex geometry.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:09.640
We will try to cover some important definitions,
axioms and postulates from

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.950
his book that will help us in solving and
proving theorems to make our

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.340
understanding of geometry clearer.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.599
So in the next lesson, we will learn about
some of the basic definitions in

00:04:21.599 --> 00:04:27.270
geometry that Euclid put in his book named
‘ELEMENTS.’

